    "circle entries report stronger formal college‑preparatory programs, measurable academic outcomes, and advanced‑course/dual‑enrollment opportunities than square entries": "This bucket emphasizes reported formal program strength plus measurable results (graduation/college matriculation, test/credit outcomes, dual‑enrollment metrics) as an outcomes‑focused complement to the already‑finalized bucket (which catalogs program offerings and curricular pathways); it is framed to be outcome/metrics‑centered and therefore distinct from the offerings‑catalog focus and from community, safety, or staff dysfunction themes.",
    "circle entries report more pervasive student-safety problems, bullying, fights, racial harassment, sexual harassment, gang activity, and administrative minimization or nonresponse than square entries": "This bucket groups concrete reports of personal and physical safety harms and the school's failure to effectively enforce or remediate them (frequent fights, racial slurs, sexual incidents, vaping, tolerated substance use, and specific claims that administration minimizes or fails to act), which is thematically different from staffing/HR dysfunction or program/community strength — it centers on student safety incidents and enforcement gaps.",
    "circle entries report more administrative and staff dysfunctional practices (unresponsiveness, nepotism/favoritism, hiring problems, inconsistent teacher quality, counseling/special‑education failures, allegations of misconduct and discriminatory discipline) than square entries": "This bucket captures systemic personnel and governance dysfunction (hiring/cronyism, favoritism, poor counselor/special‑ed practice, inconsistent grading/enforcement, discriminatory discipline, unresponsive offices) focused on how adults and policies operate — distinct from safety incidents (which are the harms) and from community/extracurricular or academic‑outcome/program reporting." 
